+# Task 1 meeting records verification
+
+Status: DONE for nonvisual local foundation; parent review/integration remains required.
+Base: c769b53bb084b0109f023f7b5f64bea7d38d3060.
+Branch: aside/meeting-records-20261028.
+
+## Owned deliverables
+- Core/Meetings/MeetingSession.cs: immutable validated snapshots, consent gating, deterministic verbatim extraction, source-note cascade.
+- Core/Meetings/MeetingStore.cs: dedicated meeting_records table via unchanged LocalSqliteStore.Open, transactional upsert, durable read, literal title/transcript search, delete and explicit retention purge.
+- Core/Meetings/MeetingExport.cs: schema-versioned timestamped JSON and escaped timestamp/source-linked Markdown strings.
+- Core.Tests/Meetings/MeetingRecordsTests.cs: 13 focused tests, disposable synthetic SQLite fixtures.
+- Exact public signatures and constraints: sibling 2026-10-28-meeting-records.md.
+
+## Test evidence
+All logs and captured process exit files are in this worktree's ignored .codex-build/meeting-evidence/.
+- red.log / red.exit: 8 failed, 2 passed; exit 1. Throwing API skeleton compiled; expected missing-behavior failures. An earlier test-target typing compilation issue was corrected before behavioral red; no production behavior was added before red.
+- search-red.log / search-red.exit: 1 failed, 12 passed; exit 1. Demonstrated raw serialized JSON cannot support literal Unicode/quoted text search; fixed by querying decoded JSON segment text with SQLite json_each/json_extract.
+- green.log / green.exit: 13 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; exit 0.
+- full-core.log / full-core.exit: 2362 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; exit 0, Release configuration. Build output has no warnings/errors.
+- git diff --check: exit 0 before commit.
+Commands: dotnet test tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests -c Release --filter FullyQualifiedName~Meetings; dotnet test tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests -c Release.
+
+The rollback test installs a real BEFORE UPDATE trigger that raises SQLite ABORT; failed replacement preserves previous source ID. This is real local-database acceptance, not a provider mock.
+
+## Limits and semantics
+- No capture, transcription engine, UI/caller integration, remote API/model, memory promotion or cloud sync. Recording is a consent-gated record state, not evidence hardware started. StartRecording is draft-only; completion can be represented by constructing a Completed snapshot.
+- Consent is caller-attested source description and timestamp, not independently verified legal consent or device identity. End-to-end recorder consent must be wired by parent.
+- Source deletion removes the segment and referencing extracts from a returned snapshot; caller must Save it. Session Delete/PurgeExpired remove durable rows. Retention is explicit caller-invoked purge, not an autonomous scheduler. Exports/backups/WAL are not securely erased.
+- Export methods return content, not files. Caller owns destination selection, atomic file persistence and UI acceptance. Export timestamp is caller-supplied. JSON exports preserve source data verbatim; Markdown escapes user-supplied syntax and HTML.
+- Notes copy all source segments exactly; action candidates require a leading ACTION: marker after whitespace. No summaries, speaker names, owner assignments, due dates or decision labels are inferred. All extracted notes/actions remain unverified candidates.
+- Search is literal, ordered by session ID and bounded to 1..100 results; title and decoded transcript text only. SQLite lower() supplies ASCII case folding, not full Unicode case normalization. Search includes expired records until explicit purge.
+- Per-field and count bounds cap finite snapshot input, not total database growth. No encrypted-at-rest guarantee or protection against a maliciously replaced local SQLite file. Store uses a new dedicated table, no edits to shared schema helper.
+- Initial record DTOs are transport values; MeetingSession construction is the validation boundary, including duplicate IDs, references and exact extract text. Read-only defensive copies prevent later collection mutation.
+- Test fixtures were synthetic, temporary and disposed; persistent full logs/exits remain only in owned ignored evidence directory. No secrets read and no personal data or hardware accessed.
+- Parent owns independent spec/code review, shell wiring, final integration gates and release.
